      "writtenOn": "2017-06-19T23:34:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We\u0027re falling into this case repeatedly on my kevin, maybe it was unnoticed because the UART isn\u0027t initialized at gpio_pre_init().\n\nI saw the previous discussion and I still don\u0027t understand. If IBBR is set under some conditions then BBRAM was unexpectedly lost -- an error print is fine, but we need to clear IBBR and try to make things work again. Otherwise IBBR will be non-functional until we hard-power-down the EC?",
